# Janssens Drone Cleaning

- Stack: Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS 4, static `output: "export"`. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using Next APIs. `LayoutProps` is generated: run `next typegen` before a bare `tsc` (`npm run typecheck` does this).
- The public brand is Janssens Drone Cleaning (JDC). The GitHub Pages basePath is `/${REPO_SLUG}` from `src/config/repo.ts` (`jdc-web`). The repository is `lodeja/jdc-web`. Do not deploy unless the owner asks. Design tokens use the `--jdc-*` prefix.
- Never invent business facts: extra services, locations, prices, certifications, testimonials, phone, email, VAT, KBO, or permits. Contact and company fields live in `src/config/business.ts` and stay null or empty until the owner fills them in. Hide a null field. Do not render TODO text.
- The five confirmed services are the list in `src/config/services.ts` (dak, gevel, ramen en glas, zonnepanelen, industrie). Each has a static page at `/${slug}/`. Do not add another service. Visible copy is Belgian Dutch (nl-BE): address the customer as u, and JDC as we. Page copy stays in `src/config/service-pages.ts`. Do not invent prices, yields, guarantees, permits, or a cleaning method the owner has not confirmed. Plaatsbezoek, testzone, osmosewater, gedemineraliseerd water, and opleverrapport are confirmed. Do not sell biologisch afbreekbaar, milieuvriendelijk, ecologisch, duurzaam, natuurlijk, or niet giftig. If a product is needed, say it is authorised in Belgium for that surface. Hydrofuge, impregneren, softwash, and voor- en nabeelden stay null in `methodNotes`.
- `/veiligheid-en-regelgeving/` describes legal duties as process. `business.compliance` stays empty until a permit, policy, or operator number is actually held. Hide empty compliance lines. Never print a euro insurance amount or claim a category JDC does not hold. Solar cleaning follows the panel manufacturer's instructions. The drone camera is GDPR: film the building, and get separate consent before using photos as references.
- Photos use the slots in `src/config/images.ts`. Until `src` is set, keep the site illustrations. No third-party stock photos.
- While `business.formEndpoint` is null, the quote form must not claim a request was sent. If `business.email` is set, a valid submit may open `mailto:` and must say the visitor still has to send it.
- Public URLs for sitemap, robots, canonical, and Open Graph come from `siteOrigin()` in `src/lib/site.ts` (`business.domain`, otherwise the GitHub Pages URL). Emit LocalBusiness JSON-LD only when `canEmitLocalBusiness()` is true. Do not add FAQPage schema. BreadcrumbList on service pages is fine.
- `/privacy/` describes only what the site does. Review it with the owner before `formEndpoint` is set. Hide controller lines that are null.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`: do not start GSAP timelines or other ongoing motion when it matches. Keep the skip link, labels, focus order, and WCAG AA contrast.
